# Live Calibration on Initial Setup's older Compass page, ported from MagCalib.DoGUIMagCalib
# (MagCalib.cs:136-790, 1271-1430) behind ConfigHWCompass's BUT_MagCalibrationLive
# (ConfigHWCompass.cs:257-261), with its window ProgressReporterSphere.
#
# The claims: the button shows Strings.MagCalibMsg, then the window; prd_DoWork turns learning off
# and zeroes the offsets (forced), asks for RAW_SENSORS at 50 Hz and takes each compass's readings
# through the near-duplicate filter onto the spheres, with "Got + N samples" and each compass's
# error in the label; Done ends the loop, "run the calibration anyway?" is asked while the coverage
# test still wants a point, Yes fits, the window closes, and SaveOffsets sends the offsets as
# PREFLIGHT_SET_SENSOR_OFFSETS, reads them back and says "These have been saved for you.", a box
# per compass, before Activate() shows the new offsets on the page.
#
# THE BUNDLED SITL CANNOT RUN THIS SCRIPT. InitialSetup lists ConfigHWCompass only for a vehicle
# without COMPASS_PRIO1_ID - ArduPilot 4.0 and earlier (InitialSetup.cs:200-207) - and the page's
# Mission Planner group only for ArduPlane 3.7.1 and later or a vehicle without onboard
# calibration (ConfigHWCompass.cs:51-70). tools/sitl holds ArduPilot 4.6, which lists
# ConfigHWCompass2, the page without Live Calibration. So this needs an ArduPlane 3.7.1-4.0 SITL,
# built from ArduPilot's Plane-4.0 branch and started through run-sitl.sh's SITL_BINARY, on
# tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 with SIM_MAG_RND 100: a simulated vehicle sits still, and without noise its
# readings fall in one filter bucket, three samples in all, which the fit's ten-sample floor
# refuses ("Log does not contain enough data"). With the noise the readings spread over a blob
# - not a sphere - so the coverage test asks the question and the offsets the fit finds are the
# blob's, not a real calibration: the SITL's offsets are rewritten, and a fresh SITL (or its
# eeprom.bin removed) puts them back. The same path runs on every build without a SITL in
# crates/mp-gui/src/config/compass.rs's live_calibration_talks_to_the_vehicle_through_the_link,
# which sends RAW_IMU readings on a sphere through the real link to a scripted autopilot.
#
#   SITL_BINARY=/path/to/arduplane-4.0 tools/sitl/run-sitl.sh plane   # with SIM_MAG_RND 100
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-compass-livecal.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one.
budget 40
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget.
expect vehicle.count > 0
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92).
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

# The page is listed once every parameter is in.
click param-download
expect params.held > 500
expect params.value.COMPASS_USE 1

click tab-setup
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigHWCompass
expect setup.page ConfigHWCompass
expect config.compass.active true
expect config.compass.class ConfigHWCompass
expect config.compass.legacy.enabled true
expect config.compass.legacy.mpcalib true
expect config.compass.livecal.open false

# The button: Strings.MagCalibMsg first, the window after it.
click compass-livecal
expect config.compass.dialog Please click ok and move the autopilot around all axises in a circular motion
expect config.compass.livecal.open false
click compass-dialog-ok
expect config.compass.dialog none
expect config.compass.livecal.open true

# prd_DoWork's writes, then the loop: learning off, the offsets zeroed, the samples arriving.
expect config.compass.livecal.phase sampling
expect params.value.COMPASS_LEARN 0
expect params.value.COMPASS_OFS_X 0
expect params.value.COMPASS_OFS_Y 0
expect params.value.COMPASS_OFS_Z 0
expect config.compass.livecal.samples1 > 20
expect config.compass.livecal.points1 > 20
expect config.compass.livecal.status ~ Got +
expect config.compass.livecal.status ~ Compass 1 error:
expect config.compass.livecal.done true
# A noise blob misses most of the sphere's twenty points: the aim points are drawn.
expect config.compass.livecal.aims > 0
expect config.compass.livecal.status ~ more data needed Aim For

# Auto accept off, then Done: the question, since points are still wanted.
click magcal-auto
click magcal-done
expect config.compass.livecal.phase asking
expect config.compass.dialog You are missing data points. do you want to run the calibration anyway?
click compass-dialog-ok

# The fit, the window closed, and the first compass's offsets sent, read back and said.
expect config.compass.livecal.open false
expect config.compass.dialog ~ New offsets for compass #1 are
expect config.compass.dialog ~ These have been saved for you.
expect config.compass.command PREFLIGHT_SET_SENSOR_OFFSETS accepted
click compass-dialog-ok
# A box for each further compass whose SCALED_IMU2 or SCALED_IMU3 carried readings, the second
# through PREFLIGHT_SET_SENSOR_OFFSETS as well, the third through its parameters. Written for a
# SITL simulating two compasses; one with a third shows its box here too, and one with a single
# compass none - adjust on the first run.
expect config.compass.dialog ~ New offsets for compass #2 are
click compass-dialog-ok
expect config.compass.jobs 0
expect config.compass.dialog none
# Activate() after the boxes: the page reads the vehicle's offsets again.
expect config.compass.legacy.1.offsets ~ OFFSETS
